      "source_example_id": "e-16538",
      "knowledge_point": "Supremum and Infimum of a Function",
      "kp_id": "e-16538"
    },
    "q-253140": {
      "dom_id": "step-q253140",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14164583/assets/b6abb4332c7601200fec40e8b3f8e6f6f8c81004aaa92af936063625a5c9f2e8.png)\n\nWhat is the infimum of the function $y=f(x)$ shown above?\n\n${inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The infimum of a function is the infimum of the range of the function.\n\nIn this case, the range of $f$ is $A=(-3,2).$\n\nTo find the infimum of a set $A,$ we must find the set containing **all** lower bounds of $A$ (i.e., the set of lower bounds) and take the maximum of this set.\n\nSo, in our case, we have that\n\n- any number $y\\le -3$ is a lower bound of $A,$\n\n- any number $y>-3$ is **not** a lower bound of $A.$ In other words, we can always find an element of $A$ that is smaller than $y$ for any $y>-3.$\n\nTherefore, $(-\\infty ,-3]$ is the set of lower bounds of $A,$ and\n\n$$\n{inf}_{x\\in R}f(x)=inf(A)=max(-\\infty ,-3]=-3.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
          "type": "blank",
          "dom_id": "freeResponseTextbox-1",
          "tag": "mathquill",
          "choices": [],
          "dom_index": 0,
          "disabled": false,
          "input_html": "<div id=\"freeResponseTextbox-1\" class=\"matheditor-wrapper-answer\" ;=\"\" style=\"min-width:35px;\n                                        margin-left:5px;\n                                        margin-right:-2px;\n                                        background:;\"><div class=\"mq-editable-field mq-math-mode\" style=\"border: none; outline: none;\"><span class=\"mq-textarea\"><textarea autocapitalize=\"off\" autocomplete=\"off\" autocorrect=\"off\" spellcheck=\"false\" x-palm-disable-ste-all=\"true\" style=\"\" disabled=\"\"></textarea></span><span class=\"mq-root-block\" mathquill-block-id=\"21\"><span mathquill-command-id=\"23\">0</span></span></div></div>",
          "rendered_text": "0",
